\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 That is sort of the point of catholicism or any such belief system - to lock in. To truly, fully encapsulate yourself into your belief that it truly seems like there is nothing that breaks it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 It becomes your new circle of world.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The moment you question it it breaks and you cannot question it and believe at the same time because belief is not even "to know" but to actually fully behave like it is truth.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 But of course, it keeps you really reluctant if not impossible to change or consider something "outside of that circle".}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Leap of faith is crucial. But then you get all kinds of tragedies and pain, like questions of mental illnesses and such problems. Basically free will problems. Whatever falls out of those circles is a huge potential tragedy because it gets excluded by your radicality.}}